// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/course/clocks-and-cdc.t27 -- the t27 course on clocking, resets and clock-domain crossings
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which reads
; it the way it reads specs/course/course.t27: the constant schema, every test block below, every
; widget in specs/widgets/gallery.t27, every lesson spec compiled clean, the Russian bundle named
; by specs/course/clocks-and-cdc-ru.t27. It writes this course into src/lib/course.generated.ts
; (the page at #/clocks-and-cdc) and a byte-identical copy of this file at
; public/learn/clocks-and-cdc.t27. ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: course 3 of specs/course/courses.t27, 27 lessons in 9 modules of 3. It
; stands on its own: what a clock is and where it enters the board, the clock tree, the MMCM,
; the three reset kinds, metastability and MTBF, crossing many bits, the asynchronous FIFO, the
; constraints file, and the crossings read back on real hardware. Every lesson opens one widget
; and one spec.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: it says no number of its own. Every number in a lesson comes from
; the spec it opens, from the recording it plays, or from the page of the widget it shows, and
; each of those names its own source. Three specs were written for this course (specs/fpga/mmcm.t27,
; specs/fpga/reset_sync.t27, specs/fpga/mtbf.t27); their teaching assumptions are labelled in the
; specs themselves, because the vendors publish flop metastability parameters only partially.
; A recording runs t27c on a real machine, plants one bug as a one-line edit, shows the test that
; fails, and puts the line back in the same recording.

; WHY 27: 3 cubed lessons, the size of a TRI-27 word. Changing the shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

